#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064281 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064125 :question/id #uuid "2bb17470-6365-5e08-b649-f9f42146a4c6" :question/math-academy-id "e-732" :question/problem "Calculate $f'(x)$ if $f(x) = 2\\sin (3x - 1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function\n\n$$\nf = 2\\sin u, \\qquad u=3x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d f}{\\textrm d u} = 2\\cos u, \\qquad\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 3.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡u \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "73216188-6524-55c3-b945-86d13ef64170" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050420} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051084}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491440 :question-generator/id #uuid "81161d7f-70af-5c80-8dcb-1391c3b4cb0e" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186064281.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064546 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc1c1e20-e0bd-5261-a228-a6393d854e62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\sin (2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061472} {:answer/id #uuid "eabd9412-f16f-51f6-9afa-a299fea0f5a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\sin (x^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061473} {:answer/id #uuid "ef240dd9-6a53-5d01-856e-e0dbfc93cd48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\sin (x^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061474} {:answer/id #uuid "3a1be5d7-ffa1-57f2-b287-c276a6a48eed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}\\sin (2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061475} {:answer/id #uuid "4eff482c-db2b-5c8c-907e-a2a93e856881" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}\\cos (x^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061476}] :answer-field/id #uuid "036a9747-914d-5a19-b770-7b65ebc0f065" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061471}] :question/id #uuid "3fce4c88-35a3-5f54-919c-8b47bd528110" :question/math-academy-id "q-1943" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{df}{dx}$ for $f(x) = \\cos (x^{2})$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064547 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d164d79-3e8a-5a0a-be16-5e01ba43a6cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\csc^{2} (2x + 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061478} {:answer/id #uuid "a7498bfe-4586-5ea2-90b0-47b5e1e0e983" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cot (2x + 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061479} {:answer/id #uuid "073354e8-10c4-5bb3-a6c9-b895b814bc8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sec^{2} (2x + 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061480} {:answer/id #uuid "0878a6d5-e68c-5cd4-8f21-d0d75793d8a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sec (2x + 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061481} {:answer/id #uuid "3bf4965c-6cb7-5099-abdd-6b4a478d4ddd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec^{2} (2x + 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061482}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4ba2a3e9-dc27-51b2-a022-1104008419eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061477}] :question/id #uuid "49ca619d-ecfe-5593-9b17-e64572a2a67e" :question/math-academy-id "q-1946" :question/problem "Find $f^{′}(x)$ for $f(x) = \\tan (2x + 2)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233773 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2998be6e-3d61-5b63-935a-7bdb143e1005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-4\\pi$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2998be6e-3d61-5b63-935a-7bdb143e1005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-4\\pi$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232538} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc5ffdb9-90bc-5cec-a6a0-95ec2b95ac7b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232537}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "390498a7-88cc-5a78-b03f-2394c5362be8" :question/math-academy-id "q-310182" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of $y =\\sin \\left(\\pi \\left(x^{2} + 2x - 2\\right)\\right)$ at $x = 1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The slope of $y = f(x)$ at $x=1$ is given by $f'(1).$\n\nWe will calculate $f'(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n\\[\ny = \\sin{u}, \\qquad u = \\pi \\left(x^{2} +2x - 2\\right).\n\\]\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} = \\cos{u}, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\pi (2x + 2).\n\\]\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n\\begin{align*}\nf'(x) &= \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x}\\\\[5pt]\n\n&=\\cos u \\cdot \\pi (2x+2)\\\\[5pt]\n\n&=\\pi (2x+2)\\cos u\\\\[5pt]\n\n&=\\pi (2x+2)\\cos \\left(  \\pi \\left(x^{2} +2x - 2\\right) \\right).\n\\end{align*}\n\nEvaluating at $x=1,$ we find\n\n\\begin{align}\nf'(1) & =\\pi (2\\cdot1+2)\\cos \\left(  \\pi \\left(1^{2} +2\\cdot1 - 2\\right) \\right) \\\\[3pt]\n\n& =4\\pi \\cos(\\pi) \\\\[3pt]\n&= 4\\pi \\cdot (-1) \\\\[3pt]\n&= -4\\pi\n\\end{align}\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of $y = f(x)$ at $x = 1$ is \n\\[\nm = f'(1) = \\bbox[4pt, border: 1px solid lightgray]{-4\\pi}.\n\\]"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233777 :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "97de5fad-6e5e-571a-91b7-dfa67983b9d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-31241" :question/problem "Find the slope of $y=\\operatorname{sin}({x}^{2}+2x-1)$ at $x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "The slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=0$ is given by ${f}^{'}(0).$\n\nWe will calculate ${f}^{'}(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}u,\\,u={x}^{2}+2x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\operatorname{cos}u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x+2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}u\\cdot (2x+2) \\\\  & =(2x+2)\\operatorname{cos}u \\\\  & =(2x+2)\\operatorname{cos}({x}^{2}+2x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=0,$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(0) & =(2\\cdot 0+2)\\operatorname{cos}({0}^{2}+2\\cdot 0-1) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}(-1) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=0$ is $2\\operatorname{cos}1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234093 :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2bc06eae-ad0a-5d3a-b849-103c9ea4b53e" :question/math-academy-id "q-48508" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y = \\cos (5x-2 )$ at the point $\\left(\\dfrac 2 5,1\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "The slope of $y = f(x)$ at $x=\\dfrac 2 5$ is given by $f'\\left(\\dfrac 2 5\\right).$\n\nWe will calculate $f'(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n\\[\ny = \\cos{u}, \\qquad u = 5x-2.\n\\]\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} = -\\sin u \\qquad \\style{font-family:inherit;}{\\text{and}} \\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 5.\n\\]\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n\\begin{align*}\nf'(x) &= \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x}\\\\[5pt]\n&=-\\sin u \\cdot 5\\\\[5pt]\n&=-5\\sin u\\\\[5pt]\n&= -5\\sin\\left(5x-2 \\right).\n\\end{align*}\n\nEvaluating at $x=\\dfrac 25,$ we find\n\n\\begin{eqnarray}\n \\eqalign{\n\nm=f'\\left(\\dfrac 25\\right)  & =- 5 \\sin \\left(5\\cdot \\dfrac 2 5-2\\right)\\\\[5pt] \n\t\t& =- 5 \\sin 0\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&= 0.\n \n       \n    }\n\\end{eqnarray}\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at the point $\\left(\\dfrac 2 5,1\\right) \\mathbin{:}$\n\n\\begin{align*}\ny-y_1&=m(x-x_1)\\\\[5pt]\ny-1&=0\\left(x-\\dfrac{2}{5}\\right)\\\\[5pt]\ny-1&=0\\\\[5pt]\ny&=1.\n\\end{align*}"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234096 :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6400ab63-050a-5a93-a765-8b1d07a079a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-48636" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $f(x) = \\cos{\\left(x^3\\right)}$ at the point $\\left(0,1\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "First, the slope of $y = f(x)$ at $x = 0$ is given by $f'(0).$\n\nWe will calculate $f'(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n\\[\ny = \\cos{u}, \\qquad u = x^3.\n\\]\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} = -\\sin{u}, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} =3x^2.\n\\]\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} &= \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x}\\\\[5pt]\n\n&= -\\sin{u} \\cdot 3x^2\\\\[5pt]\n\n&=-3x^2\\sin(x^3).\n\\end{align*}\n\nEvaluating at $x=0,$ we find\n\\begin{align}\nm=f'(0) & = -3(0)^2\\sin(0^3) = 0.\n\\end{align}\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at the point $(0,1) \\mathbin{:}$\n\\begin{align}\ny - y_1 & = m(x - x_1)\\\\[3pt]\n\ny - 1 & = 0 \\cdot \\left(x - 0 \\right)\\\\[3pt]\n\ny - 1 & = 0\\\\[3pt]\n\ny & =1.\n\\end{align}"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297322 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c11aa0cd-50a9-55f9-b43c-ec6085afea6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{x}^{3}{sec}^{2}(3{x}^{4}-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296287} {:answer/id #uuid "b2066b38-d1dc-4961-8caa-0b613f496873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12x^3\\sec^2\\left(3x^4-5\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c11aa0cd-50a9-55f9-b43c-ec6085afea6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{x}^{3}{sec}^{2}(3{x}^{4}-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296287} :answer-field/id #uuid "41d54636-77f2-54cb-a399-2372401bb451" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296758}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a87f80fe-d2d2-50e5-bf92-8b685bd67b58" :question/math-academy-id "q-310179" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3{x}^{4}-5)$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as a composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡u,\\,u=3{x}^{4}-5.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}={sec}^{2}⁡u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=12{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot 12{x}^{3} \\\\  & =12{x}^{3}{sec}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =12{x}^{3}{sec}^{2}⁡(3{x}^{4}-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297323 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e6eb30f-5bfc-5e1d-a01c-0f6eb7e00e8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e6eb30f-5bfc-5e1d-a01c-0f6eb7e00e8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295719} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8643e81-9ec6-59f8-9881-f0c74f9799e1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4c450049-c1ac-524d-8d79-0a2c2ad034fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-310180" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is given by ${f}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right).$\n\nWe will calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,u=3x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is \n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)=0.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297328 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d50494a-917e-5fc9-aaca-421ef13620f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295342} {:answer/id #uuid "3aba53ad-193b-5d70-873b-c0e3c7c67902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295604} {:answer/id #uuid "cf3a18b3-703f-5be8-adc1-aabd15547f90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296355} {:answer/id #uuid "d11f2b61-41fa-5a40-9644-c5fb5f1d15b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296366} {:answer/id #uuid "fba457fb-4dfa-5ba5-ab35-1a6884267105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296608}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d50494a-917e-5fc9-aaca-421ef13620f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295342} :answer-field/id #uuid "b67cf090-cb84-5901-9453-1f707812d0f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d3355be-a5a0-56e5-8db1-b9c9b33d002a" :question/math-academy-id "q-31153" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)$ at the point where $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=2$ is given by ${f}^{′}(2).$\n\nWe will calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,u=3x+5.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=2,$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(2) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 2+5) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡11.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=2$ is $3\\operatorname{cos}⁡11.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297329 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "839fa6c2-077d-5ff2-ac87-202c88b24d73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11-2x)-9{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295972} {:answer/id #uuid "845a86c6-af92-5003-9e84-abb01c1b1037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11-2x)-9{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295976} {:answer/id #uuid "ae90c9d3-49ef-5560-b2b9-97ed8b3e467b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11-2x)-18{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296188} {:answer/id #uuid "e92d5c94-4ae2-53dc-bf2b-f28a16b6d315" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11-2x)-18{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296508} {:answer/id #uuid "e99e59dc-3c45-58f0-abbc-809678feb2fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11-2x)-18{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e99e59dc-3c45-58f0-abbc-809678feb2fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11-2x)-18{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296511} :answer-field/id #uuid "e16ad6c1-d476-5dae-b48f-bee5ac9ba27e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297098}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a15a3bf2-ccf2-5108-b6fe-372cf79c1d17" :question/math-academy-id "q-31163" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11-2x)-6{x}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11-2x)$ and $h(x)=-6{x}^{3}.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =g(x)+h(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we differentiate $g(x).$ We express $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11-2x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ng=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,u=11-2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}u}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11-2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate $h(x)=-6{x}^{3}.$ \n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x}=-18{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)={g}^{′}(x)+{h}^{′}(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11-2x)-18{x}^{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332841 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3975e3e3-190d-50c6-a1fa-2372d4812b2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x-\\pi -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330465} {:answer/id #uuid "86d8dbc9-4448-5893-85ef-2de9fe4cbe8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x+\\pi -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331151} {:answer/id #uuid "8cb1a78b-64dd-5b14-bc5f-ce06a27bb9ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331200} {:answer/id #uuid "9617b878-c4f0-5d98-8d9b-dbb4117349ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x+2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331282} {:answer/id #uuid "afe48e27-93ba-5a98-8584-1499283d0a82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cb1a78b-64dd-5b14-bc5f-ce06a27bb9ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331200} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d979568-c652-583d-8844-6e678e24e5e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332303}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9ea4e0db-90cb-5911-bc10-79d17635a4f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-51026" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)$ at the point $(1+\\pi ,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=1+\\pi $ is given by ${f}^{′}(1+\\pi ).$\n\nWe will calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,u=x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=1+\\pi ,$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(1+\\pi ) & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1+\\pi -1) \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at the point $(1+\\pi ,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-2) & =0(x-(1+\\pi )) \\\\ y+2 & =0 \\\\ y & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491422 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c21bebd-faa9-5e47-86d5-105935cf93a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491413} {:answer/id #uuid "8609c4ba-b913-512c-b515-0998e93e7785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- 12 x + 12 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491415} {:answer/id #uuid "e306351b-f7b2-5a3a-a137-067728da4a2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x - 13 - \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491429} {:answer/id #uuid "e6f5eaf7-7a98-5396-8b85-e5a1ae4f1cf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491430} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e39cff-3a0b-561b-aed8-6264adb9a14b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x - 12 + \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6f5eaf7-7a98-5396-8b85-e5a1ae4f1cf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491430} :answer-field/id #uuid "fffaf1e8-370e-5f04-8dfc-a0db9cc43904" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/id